WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club

﻿1

00:01:44.917 --> 00:01:46.542
Told you I'd find it.


00:01:47.294 --> 00:01:48.919
But not if they found it first.


00:01:50.964 --> 00:01:52.381
I doubt it.


00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:56.675
It looks to me like that crocodile
won't have to feed for a while.


00:02:21.829 --> 00:02:22.954
And to think you,


00:02:23.121 --> 00:02:25.330
and everyone, doubted me.


00:02:25.958 --> 00:02:29.458
You know, I don't even know why
I let you come, Brother…


00:02:33.882 --> 00:02:36.382
I'm sure you'll think of a reason.


00:02:54.861 --> 00:02:57.069
The Hamster of Darkness.


00:02:58.656 --> 00:02:59.781
Finally.


00:02:59.949 --> 00:03:02.032
And when I bring this back
to the kingdom,


00:03:02.202 --> 00:03:05.119
nobody's going to be laughing
at my ear anymore.


00:03:05.288 --> 00:03:06.288
No,


00:03:06.456 --> 00:03:08.998
I'm going to be the one
who's laughing…


00:03:09.167 --> 00:03:10.667
not at my ear of course.


00:03:10.835 --> 00:03:12.585
But because I was right,


00:03:12.754 --> 00:03:15.129
that the hamster is real.


00:03:21.888 --> 00:03:23.679
Something does not feel right.


00:03:23.848 --> 00:03:25.056
Oh hush,


00:03:25.225 --> 00:03:28.683
let me enjoy
this glorious moment.


00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:49.203
<i>Twenty years ago my father
and his brother Lapin</i>


00:03:49.373 --> 00:03:52.415
<i>almost found the greatest
artifact in the world.</i>


00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:55.336
I'm sorry, Lapin.


00:03:56.005 --> 00:03:57.422
This isn't happening.


00:03:58.382 --> 00:04:00.465
- What the…?
- Over there.


00:04:00.885 --> 00:04:03.135
<i>But they found something else…</i>


00:04:06.891 --> 00:04:07.891
<i>Me.</i>


00:04:13.189 --> 00:04:14.355
What is it?


00:04:16.943 --> 00:04:18.484
The little freak's
pointing at my ear!


00:04:18.986 --> 00:04:20.361
No, he's not.


00:04:20.697 --> 00:04:22.322
He did it again!


00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.990
Nonsense. He's adorable.


00:04:25.576 --> 00:04:26.951
Hi there, little guy.


00:04:27.203 --> 00:04:28.869
You're not taking him back with us?


00:04:29.038 --> 00:04:30.080
I'm not leaving him.


00:04:30.539 --> 00:04:33.539
Good thing I'm the older brother
and will be king someday,


00:04:33.709 --> 00:04:35.125
because you're too soft, Brother!


00:04:35.294 --> 00:04:37.169
Way too soft!


00:04:38.172 --> 00:04:40.214
<i>My uncle never found
the Hamster of Darkness.</i>


00:04:40.382 --> 00:04:42.132
<i>And he was never named king.</i>


00:04:42.301 --> 00:04:44.676
<i>But we'll get to that soon enough…</i>


00:05:17.253 --> 00:05:19.628
<i>From the moment
my dad brought me home,</i>


00:05:19.796 --> 00:05:21.546
<i>I was preparing for the day</i>


00:05:21.715 --> 00:05:24.673
<i>when I would become
a great adventurer like him.</i>


00:05:29.931 --> 00:05:31.265
There you go.


00:05:37.231 --> 00:05:39.523
Nice slap of the wrist.


00:05:46.907 --> 00:05:48.407
What do you think?


00:05:53.246 --> 00:05:55.371
<i>My favorite days were the days</i>


00:05:55.541 --> 00:05:58.082
<i>when my dad returned
from an adventure…</i>


00:05:59.503 --> 00:06:01.586
Personally, I don't see
what the big deal is…


00:06:01.755 --> 00:06:03.505
I mean, they just found old junk.


00:06:03.674 --> 00:06:07.382
I find old junk in alleys
and nobody's throwing me a parade.


00:06:07.719 --> 00:06:09.719
That's my turtle servant Abe.


00:06:09.888 --> 00:06:12.596
He's a "glass-is-all-empty" kind of guy.


00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:16.392
- Dad!
- Hi there, little guy.


00:06:16.562 --> 00:06:18.895
Did you find the fork
from the last brunch?


00:06:19.064 --> 00:06:21.064
And the knife!


00:06:21.399 --> 00:06:24.941
But I couldn't find the spoon!


00:06:25.111 --> 00:06:27.028
Of course, I found the spoon!


00:06:33.119 --> 00:06:36.994
<i>When I saw how everyone looked up
to adventurers like my dad,</i>


00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:42.415
<i>there and then I decided
that's how I wanted them to see me.</i>


00:06:46.632 --> 00:06:50.966
And so there I was, 200 feet
above hare-eating crocodiles,


00:06:51.137 --> 00:06:53.429
hanging from a cliff.


00:06:53.807 --> 00:06:55.974
- And then what happened?
- And then…


00:07:00.063 --> 00:07:01.480
you went to bed.


00:07:03.108 --> 00:07:05.983
That's why they call it
a cliffhanger, pal.


00:07:06.152 --> 00:07:09.777
Good night,
my future royal adventurer.


00:07:27.465 --> 00:07:29.382
<i>I was obsessed with adventuring.</i>


00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:31.967
<i>I stayed up every night reading.</i>


00:07:39.602 --> 00:07:41.435
Stupid feathers…


00:07:46.984 --> 00:07:51.401
<i>I devoured every book about adventuring
and spent hours in the royal library…</i>


00:07:51.947 --> 00:07:55.197
<i>I could not get enough of it.
I knew the day would come.</i>


00:08:08.255 --> 00:08:11.630
I don't think heavy lifting
is in my job description.


00:08:29.569 --> 00:08:32.194
The tryouts, let's go, Abe.


00:08:55.635 --> 00:08:59.344
<i>Every year I watched
the Royal Adventure Society tryouts,</i>


00:08:59.932 --> 00:09:02.557
<i>determined to pick up tips
for when it was my turn to run.</i>


00:09:05.855 --> 00:09:07.771
Why'd you invite him to sit with us?


00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:11.315
My dad made me
'cause his dad's the new king.


00:09:11.485 --> 00:09:14.110
I can't believe we gotta be seen
with that freak Chickenhare.


00:09:14.279 --> 00:09:15.279
It could be worse.


00:09:15.739 --> 00:09:17.822
We could be Chickenhare.


00:09:18.908 --> 00:09:20.575
- Right?
- Oh man.


00:10:04.371 --> 00:10:05.663
That was a lot of fun.


00:10:06.205 --> 00:10:07.247
What a crock,


00:10:07.416 --> 00:10:10.707
the competitors are getting
better and better every year.


00:10:10.877 --> 00:10:13.002
- Some world classic…
- Chickenhare?


00:10:15.006 --> 00:10:16.173
What are you wearing?


00:10:17.175 --> 00:10:19.425
Like it? It's very in.


00:10:19.594 --> 00:10:22.011
It's very now… now.


00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:26.638
Boots that make you look like
you have hare feet are very now… now?


00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:29.685
Style's changed a lot since
you were a kid, Dad.


00:10:29.854 --> 00:10:32.438
Come on,
let's take that hat off so I can…


00:10:32.607 --> 00:10:33.649
No!


00:10:33.817 --> 00:10:36.150
Everybody laughs at me, Dad.


00:10:36.319 --> 00:10:39.444
I know it's hard being different.


00:10:39.823 --> 00:10:43.489
No, you don't know.
Nobody knows what it's like to be me.


00:10:44.452 --> 00:10:47.410
Chickenhare,
now what have I always told you?


00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:50.080
The things that make us different…


00:10:50.249 --> 00:10:52.499
Are the things that make us special.


00:10:52.919 --> 00:10:55.627
Yeah, I know, Dad.
But I don't wanna be special.


00:10:55.797 --> 00:10:57.630
I just wanna be normal.


00:10:58.632 --> 00:10:59.841
And wearing this,


00:11:00.719 --> 00:11:02.594
I feel normal.


00:11:04.513 --> 00:11:08.222
Maybe I'm not as up
on the fashion trends as I used to be.


00:11:08.977 --> 00:11:10.643
It's not just you, Dad!


00:11:10.812 --> 00:11:12.395
It's all old people.


00:11:13.314 --> 00:11:15.397
And check out what I can do
in my new boots.


00:11:20.821 --> 00:11:21.988
I'm okay.


00:11:22.156 --> 00:11:23.156
All good…


00:11:23.532 --> 00:11:24.741
Little sore, but good.


00:11:24.909 --> 00:11:27.326
It's just a phase.
He'll grow out of it.


00:12:02.029 --> 00:12:04.862
This is it, Abe. Moment of truth.


00:12:05.032 --> 00:12:07.282
The day all my dreams come true.


00:12:07.451 --> 00:12:10.160
Remember my three keys to success?


00:12:10.329 --> 00:12:13.329
Don't. Screw. Up.


00:12:14.207 --> 00:12:16.582
In accordance with the laws
in the Royal Rulebook,


00:12:16.752 --> 00:12:19.835
those applicants today
who reach the finish line


00:12:20.005 --> 00:12:24.963
shall be considered for
the Royal Adventure Society for life.


00:12:25.594 --> 00:12:27.719
First up, Chickenhare.


00:12:40.233 --> 00:12:42.358
This should be interesting!


00:12:57.375 --> 00:12:58.750
Come on!


00:13:06.551 --> 00:13:08.009
That's just slowing me down.


00:13:08.178 --> 00:13:09.178
What are you doing?


00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:28.114
Ouch, that hurts.


00:13:34.204 --> 00:13:35.912
Just getting my bearings.


00:13:36.456 --> 00:13:38.581
Time to make up some ground.


00:13:54.432 --> 00:13:55.432
Here we go.


00:14:06.236 --> 00:14:08.278
I'm okay, I'm okay.
Just go on.


00:14:16.162 --> 00:14:17.162
Sorry!


00:14:34.138 --> 00:14:35.346
Hey, that's cheating!


00:14:55.743 --> 00:14:56.743
Come on.


00:14:56.911 --> 00:14:58.036
You're almost there.


00:14:58.204 --> 00:15:01.579
All you have to do is get across
the Really-Really-Deep-


00:15:01.749 --> 00:15:04.749
But-Not-Quite-Bottomless-Pit.


00:15:08.505 --> 00:15:09.922
Careful, Son.


00:15:10.717 --> 00:15:13.675
I can't watch,
but I can't look away.


00:15:20.017 --> 00:15:21.017
Easy.


00:15:27.108 --> 00:15:28.191
- Come here.
- Let it go!


00:15:55.552 --> 00:15:58.886
- Well, there's always a plan B.
- I don't have a plan B.


00:15:59.056 --> 00:16:01.181
You could become a stamp collector.


00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:04.183
Yeah, it's like an adventure
every time the mail comes.


00:16:04.353 --> 00:16:07.853
And the mail comes every day.
That's a lot of adventures.


00:16:08.482 --> 00:16:12.524
What's so great about being
a royal adventurer anyway?


00:16:12.694 --> 00:16:14.319
Besides the fame and adulation?


00:16:14.488 --> 00:16:17.238
Hey, Chickenhare, nice work today!


00:16:17.408 --> 00:16:19.116
Nothing but net!


00:16:20.411 --> 00:16:23.494
What'd you expect?
He's mostly chicken.


00:16:23.914 --> 00:16:25.330
No, he's mostly hare.


00:16:25.499 --> 00:16:26.582
- Chicken!
- Hare!


00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:28.292
- Chicken!
- Hare!


00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:32.002
You know, if you close your eyes
and take it out of context,


00:16:32.172 --> 00:16:34.213
it sounds like
they're cheering for you.


00:16:34.383 --> 00:16:36.591
Chicken! Hare! Chicken! Hare!


00:16:37.678 --> 00:16:38.761
Chicken…


00:16:44.851 --> 00:16:47.476
Why can't I be like everyone else?


00:16:47.813 --> 00:16:49.104
Chickenhare?


00:16:49.272 --> 00:16:51.230
Geez, Dad, think you could knock?


00:16:52.233 --> 00:16:53.233
Sorry.


00:16:53.401 --> 00:16:56.109
Thought you'd want to talk
about what happened today.


00:16:56.279 --> 00:16:57.654
Oh, that.


00:16:58.323 --> 00:17:00.114
Just a minor setback is all.


00:17:00.408 --> 00:17:03.075
Next year, I'm gonna focus
on doing more cardio.


00:17:03.244 --> 00:17:05.536
Maybe some altitude training.


00:17:05.706 --> 00:17:08.247
You do know you can't audition twice.


00:17:08.416 --> 00:17:11.999
Well I figured since you're the King,
you could make an exception.


00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:15.087
I can't break the rules
just because you're my son.


00:17:15.506 --> 00:17:16.715
Come on, Dad.


00:17:16.883 --> 00:17:19.717
All I need is one more shot.
I know I could crush it…


00:17:19.886 --> 00:17:22.595
Chickenhare, you need
to put your energies elsewhere.


00:17:26.852 --> 00:17:30.810
I know it's difficult
to let go of your dream.


00:17:30.981 --> 00:17:33.772
I just don't want
to see you get hurt again.


00:17:35.235 --> 00:17:37.443
Is this because I embarrassed you?


00:17:37.988 --> 00:17:41.404
Chickenhare.
You could never embarrass me.


00:17:41.574 --> 00:17:45.657
When I look at you,
I wish you could see what I see.


00:17:45.828 --> 00:17:47.661
Yeah, wish I could too.


00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:51.455
All I see is that I got the worst parts
of a hare and a chicken.


00:17:51.626 --> 00:17:53.917
Maybe you got the best parts.


00:17:54.087 --> 00:17:55.587
Do you know


00:17:55.755 --> 00:17:58.546
the greatest treasure I ever found?


00:17:58.924 --> 00:18:00.883
The Fountain of Middle Age?


00:18:01.052 --> 00:18:02.469
It was you.


00:18:02.637 --> 00:18:07.387
Finding you when Uncle Lapin and I went
searching for the Hamster of Darkness


00:18:07.558 --> 00:18:10.225
was the best thing
that ever happened to me.


00:18:11.437 --> 00:18:12.771
Goodnight, Son.


00:18:28.204 --> 00:18:29.746
Oh, shut up!


00:18:31.916 --> 00:18:33.291
I've studied adventuring


00:18:33.459 --> 00:18:35.001
more than anybody, right?


00:18:35.795 --> 00:18:39.878
I've gotta figure out the location
of the treasure that every adventurer


00:18:40.049 --> 00:18:42.632
has been searching for,
but has never found…


00:18:47.348 --> 00:18:49.015
And when I figure that out,


00:18:49.183 --> 00:18:52.058
he'll have to let me
into the Royal Adventurer Society.


00:18:54.897 --> 00:18:55.897
What's the treasure?


00:18:56.482 --> 00:18:59.149
Come on,
you know what I'm talking about.


00:18:59.318 --> 00:19:02.193
The greatest
undiscovered treasure of all time…


00:19:02.362 --> 00:19:05.904
Gotcha. The greatest
undiscovered treasure of all time.


00:19:06.366 --> 00:19:07.366
I have no idea.


00:19:07.952 --> 00:19:11.535
Arturo the Rodent King created it
to take over the world.


00:19:11.956 --> 00:19:13.206
Nope. Doesn't ring a bell.


00:19:13.373 --> 00:19:15.748
Then his brother Ramon
stole it and hid it


00:19:15.918 --> 00:19:17.918
before Arturo could use it.


00:19:18.879 --> 00:19:21.879
It's got the power
of a million hamsters!


00:19:24.176 --> 00:19:25.926
Nope, still don't have it.


00:19:26.345 --> 00:19:28.886
It rhymes
with the "Damster of Harkness".


00:19:34.854 --> 00:19:38.312
The Hamster of Darkness, Abe!
How could you not get that?


00:19:38.648 --> 00:19:41.440
From where I'm sitting,
it was a problem with the clues.


00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:43.443
According to the old legends,


00:19:43.612 --> 00:19:45.737
"At the hour of 9
on a new day's dawn,


00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:49.198
"the constellation
of the hamster shall point


00:19:49.368 --> 00:19:51.576
"to The Temple
of the Hamster of Darkness."


00:19:51.745 --> 00:19:53.161
Well, it's almost 9


00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:55.913
which means I'm about
to make time-and-a-half.


00:19:57.042 --> 00:19:58.334
There's just one problem.


00:19:58.502 --> 00:20:00.960
You can't see a constellation
at 9 in the morning.


00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:02.213
It's too bright out.


00:20:02.381 --> 00:20:05.089
- We gotta be missing something.
- Yeah, breakfast.


00:20:05.384 --> 00:20:07.300
- I'm starving!
- I need the original text.


00:20:20.149 --> 00:20:22.274
<i>Erik the Literal's Volume 13</i>


00:20:22.442 --> 00:20:24.942
on the Hamster of Darkness
is checked out.


00:20:25.362 --> 00:20:26.445
When's it due back?


00:20:27.071 --> 00:20:28.571
Three months ago.


00:20:29.366 --> 00:20:32.366
Fine, I'll go get it myself.
So, who's got it?


00:20:33.036 --> 00:20:34.869
Your Uncle Lapin.


00:20:39.459 --> 00:20:43.209
So how long has it been
since you've seen your uncle?


00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:46.047
Not since he tried
to overthrow my father.


00:20:46.215 --> 00:20:50.007
He wasn't happy that my grandfather
chose my dad as king and not him.


00:20:50.178 --> 00:20:52.094
Talk about rich people's problems.


00:20:52.263 --> 00:20:53.513
Let's go.


00:20:53.682 --> 00:20:55.057
I'm sure time has mellowed him.


00:20:55.224 --> 00:20:57.266
Oh no.
My duties as your turtleservant


00:20:57.436 --> 00:20:59.352
do not extend to accompanying you


00:20:59.521 --> 00:21:02.563
to meet with your terrifying uncle
in his jail cell.


00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:06.983
Nothing about meeting
with evil uncles in their jail cells…


00:21:07.696 --> 00:21:09.654
See, this is why you join a union.


00:21:09.823 --> 00:21:12.531
Servants-and-Bed-Pan-Handlers Local 645.


00:21:12.701 --> 00:21:14.701
Strength through numbers.


00:21:36.933 --> 00:21:37.933
What's he in for?


00:21:38.267 --> 00:21:39.267
Murder.


00:21:39.602 --> 00:21:40.602
Tax evasion.


00:21:41.270 --> 00:21:43.354
I murdered the tax code.


00:21:44.315 --> 00:21:48.523
The prison that can hold Barry Goldfarb
hasn't been built!


00:21:49.946 --> 00:21:51.238
Some rules to remember:


00:21:51.405 --> 00:21:54.697
Do not pass Lapin anything
as he will turn it into a weapon,


00:21:54.868 --> 00:21:56.076
even a carrot.


00:21:56.244 --> 00:21:58.619
Do not approach his cell.
Do not touch the bars.


00:21:58.788 --> 00:22:00.872
And whatever you do,
don't reach through the bars.


00:22:01.040 --> 00:22:03.874
The last guy to do that
spent a month in the hospital.


00:22:04.043 --> 00:22:08.085
Granted that was for the flu.
But I'm sure he caught it from Lapin.


00:22:09.715 --> 00:22:10.965
You're not coming with me?


00:22:11.134 --> 00:22:14.300
The union says I don't have to.
Thank goodness


00:22:14.470 --> 00:22:17.387
for Prison-Guards-and-Haberdashers
Local 646.


00:22:17.556 --> 00:22:19.348
Strength through numbers.


00:22:48.086 --> 00:22:49.086
Nephew?


00:22:50.130 --> 00:22:52.005
What a pleasant surprise.


00:22:52.550 --> 00:22:53.883
Hi, Uncle Lapin.


00:22:54.051 --> 00:22:57.592
I was in the neighborhood
and thought it might be nice


00:22:58.221 --> 00:23:01.096
to stop by and say "hi".


00:23:01.434 --> 00:23:02.434
So…


00:23:02.893 --> 00:23:03.893
Hi!


00:23:04.812 --> 00:23:05.895
And oh yeah,


00:23:06.063 --> 00:23:08.688
there's this book
that you've got from the library.


00:23:08.857 --> 00:23:10.816
It's actually long overdue.


00:23:11.652 --> 00:23:13.860
Oh no.
What are they gonna do,


00:23:14.029 --> 00:23:15.112
lock me up?


00:23:17.700 --> 00:23:18.783
Right.


00:23:19.117 --> 00:23:21.659
That's funny because
you're already locked up


00:23:21.829 --> 00:23:23.745
for trying to overthrow my father.


00:23:23.914 --> 00:23:27.039
Well, I always did have a problem
with authority.


00:23:27.209 --> 00:23:30.542
So, you're looking
for the Hamster of Darkness,


00:23:30.879 --> 00:23:31.879
are you?


00:23:33.340 --> 00:23:34.756
I don't think it's real.


00:23:34.925 --> 00:23:35.925
Really?


00:23:36.927 --> 00:23:39.844
Every time I've requested a book
on the topic of adventuring


00:23:40.013 --> 00:23:43.597
and it wasn't in,
it was because you had checked it out.


00:23:44.267 --> 00:23:46.809
Somebody's been doing
their homework.


00:23:46.979 --> 00:23:49.895
It's real. And we both know it.


00:23:50.357 --> 00:23:52.857
It'd be quite a feather
in your cap to bring back


00:23:53.026 --> 00:23:56.651
to the Royal Adventure Society,
wouldn't it?


00:23:57.364 --> 00:23:58.530
Maybe…


00:23:59.867 --> 00:24:01.242
Such a waste.


00:24:01.409 --> 00:24:03.951
You see, when I find
the Hamster of Darkness,


00:24:04.121 --> 00:24:06.912
I'm going to use it
to take over the kingdom.


00:24:09.542 --> 00:24:10.626
I'm just joking.


00:24:10.793 --> 00:24:13.418
Besides, I'm locked in this tower


00:24:13.588 --> 00:24:16.463
that no one has ever escaped from.


00:24:16.633 --> 00:24:17.966
You think I've been waiting here,


00:24:18.135 --> 00:24:21.551
hoping you'd visit because you were
the final piece of my escape plan?


00:24:22.847 --> 00:24:25.180
I wish I was that cunning.
But now…


00:24:25.850 --> 00:24:28.183
let me find that book for you.


00:24:29.229 --> 00:24:31.521
Is this the one?


00:24:31.898 --> 00:24:33.981
Oh yeah, that's the one.


00:24:34.776 --> 00:24:37.151
So, if you'd just toss it on over here,


00:24:37.320 --> 00:24:41.112
I'll get out of your way
and you can go back


00:24:41.574 --> 00:24:44.116
to marking the days
on the wall with chalk.


00:24:44.494 --> 00:24:49.077
I'm afraid my time in here
has weakened me.


00:24:49.749 --> 00:24:51.416
Come over here.


00:24:52.001 --> 00:24:55.209
Why not just give it a little toss?


00:24:58.175 --> 00:24:59.591
On second thought,


00:24:59.926 --> 00:25:01.092
I'll come get it.


00:25:12.980 --> 00:25:15.314
Hold on.
I just remembered…


00:25:15.692 --> 00:25:16.900
I'm not done with it.


00:25:20.237 --> 00:25:22.446
Goodbye, Chickenhare.


00:25:22.615 --> 00:25:24.532
Don't forget your hat.


00:25:53.104 --> 00:25:54.312
Oh no…


00:26:00.361 --> 00:26:04.736
"Dear Brother,
enjoy your last days as king.


00:26:04.907 --> 00:26:06.741
"All the best, Lapin."


00:26:06.909 --> 00:26:08.576
I'm sorry, Dad.


00:26:08.745 --> 00:26:11.495
You know you're not allowed
to visit Lapin!


00:26:11.789 --> 00:26:12.956
What were you thinking?


00:26:13.124 --> 00:26:16.082
He had this book I needed
about the Hamster of Darkness.


00:26:16.252 --> 00:26:19.168
- See I figured…
- I told you to let it go.


00:26:20.256 --> 00:26:21.589
Sir, it's a map!


00:26:23.134 --> 00:26:25.550
"The Tomb of the Unknown Turtle"?


00:26:25.719 --> 00:26:29.219
The ancient adventurer Frederic
the Extremely Short proposed that


00:26:29.556 --> 00:26:32.056
as one of the rumored locations
of the Hamster of Darkness.


00:26:32.309 --> 00:26:33.893
That's where Lapin's going.


00:26:34.061 --> 00:26:35.978
Ready my fastest boat.
We leave immediately.


00:26:37.940 --> 00:26:40.982
Dad, I know everything
about the Hamster of Darkness.


00:26:41.152 --> 00:26:42.277
Bring me along, I can help.


00:26:42.653 --> 00:26:45.319
No. You've done enough already.


00:27:09.680 --> 00:27:12.555
Hey, Boss, just came by
to see how you're doing.


00:27:12.724 --> 00:27:15.724
Other than letting the Kingdom's
most dangerous criminal escape.


00:27:15.894 --> 00:27:17.436
- I'm doing great.
- You are?


00:27:17.604 --> 00:27:20.729
- Look what was behind the bookshelf.
- An abstract painting?


00:27:21.358 --> 00:27:22.358
A map, Abe.


00:27:23.652 --> 00:27:26.194
Lapin's been obsessed
with the Hamster of Darkness.


00:27:26.363 --> 00:27:27.905
It doesn't make sense
that he'd think


00:27:28.073 --> 00:27:30.781
the Temple would be
at the Tomb of the Unknown Turtle.


00:27:31.201 --> 00:27:33.159
That's been searched so many times.


00:27:33.912 --> 00:27:35.745
It's a minute before 9,


00:27:36.289 --> 00:27:37.581
something's missing.


00:27:38.083 --> 00:27:41.083
The moths are gonna be
the only ones to miss Lapin.


00:27:41.252 --> 00:27:42.627
It's winter.


00:27:42.796 --> 00:27:44.379
There are no moths.


00:27:46.007 --> 00:27:47.466
It's the constellation!


00:27:48.259 --> 00:27:49.259
Coincidence.


00:27:49.427 --> 00:27:50.510
It's not, Abe.


00:27:50.679 --> 00:27:52.971
Lapin has been on his quest for years.


00:27:53.139 --> 00:27:55.931
It's not a blanket,
it's a curtain, give me that.


00:28:00.731 --> 00:28:02.814
You see, total coincidence.


00:28:03.108 --> 00:28:04.858
I'm not so sure.


00:28:05.276 --> 00:28:06.526
Let me clear the floor.


00:28:06.695 --> 00:28:07.903
Yes, that's it!


00:28:08.071 --> 00:28:09.154
The book.


00:28:14.535 --> 00:28:17.577
"At the hour of 9
on a new day's dawn,


00:28:17.956 --> 00:28:19.664
"the constellation shall point


00:28:20.166 --> 00:28:22.833
"to The Temple
of the Hamster of Darkness."


00:28:44.649 --> 00:28:45.982
Bingo.


00:28:46.526 --> 00:28:49.651
Where's the "X"? Don't maps need
an "X" to mark the spot?


00:28:51.739 --> 00:28:53.864
Oh, darn tropes.


00:28:57.912 --> 00:28:59.578
Dad! Wait!


00:28:59.747 --> 00:29:01.622
You're going the wrong way!


00:29:05.044 --> 00:29:06.835
We need to get a boat ready.


00:29:07.004 --> 00:29:09.921
We have to beat Lapin
to the Hamster of Darkness.


00:29:10.090 --> 00:29:13.299
Oh no, forget about it.
I am not an adventurer.


00:29:13.469 --> 00:29:16.261
And you're…
How do I put this delicately?


00:29:16.431 --> 00:29:18.097
You're… you.


00:29:18.266 --> 00:29:20.058
Maybe I'm not much of an adventurer,


00:29:20.226 --> 00:29:22.601
but we're the only ones
who can do this now.


00:29:22.895 --> 00:29:24.395
And if we don't,


00:29:24.564 --> 00:29:27.272
Lapin's gonna come back
and take over the Kingdom.


00:29:27.567 --> 00:29:29.817
Well, unemployment is kinda high.


00:29:29.985 --> 00:29:32.319
And your dad's been king for what?
15 years?


00:29:32.488 --> 00:29:34.905
This is serious, Abe.
And it's all my fault.


00:29:35.491 --> 00:29:37.825
Not all. Only like 90%.


00:29:38.077 --> 00:29:40.368
I'm going.
And I want you to come with me.


00:29:40.663 --> 00:29:43.371
I'm your royal servant.
I'm legally bound to go with you.


00:29:43.833 --> 00:29:47.499
No. I'm not asking as your master.


00:29:47.962 --> 00:29:49.712
I'm asking you as a friend.


00:29:49.880 --> 00:29:51.547
That makes it an easy decision.


00:29:54.134 --> 00:29:57.468
Actually, that makes it
an incredibly difficult decision.


00:29:57.638 --> 00:29:59.180
Can you be friends with your boss?


00:29:59.890 --> 00:30:03.182
Isn't the relationship completely skewed
by the power dynamic?


00:30:03.352 --> 00:30:04.352
What?


00:30:04.519 --> 00:30:06.144
These are deep questions.


00:30:06.313 --> 00:30:09.105
I, for one, find them
intellectually invigorating.


00:30:09.274 --> 00:30:11.024
Wait, wait.


00:30:11.401 --> 00:30:12.776
Actually, I'm sorry,
keep going.


00:30:13.654 --> 00:30:14.654
Wait.


00:30:16.323 --> 00:30:17.365
I'm coming…


00:30:17.532 --> 00:30:18.741
friend.


00:30:18.909 --> 00:30:21.534
But be prepared
for a lot of "I told you so's."


00:30:28.168 --> 00:30:32.710
<i>I have been at sea
for 12 long minutes.</i>


00:30:32.882 --> 00:30:34.715
<i>The heat is unbearable.</i>


00:30:35.050 --> 00:30:37.384
<i>Thirst is a constant companion.</i>


00:30:37.552 --> 00:30:39.177
<i>And as for hunger,</i>


00:30:39.346 --> 00:30:43.388
<i>I may be developing
a taste for chicken and hare.</i>


00:30:47.938 --> 00:30:49.647
Not too late to turn around.


00:30:50.107 --> 00:30:51.857
I always wanted an adventure.


00:30:52.026 --> 00:30:54.484
I just hope we can pull it off.


00:30:54.653 --> 00:30:55.903
I'm sure we will.


00:30:58.991 --> 00:31:01.991
<i>I have no confidence
in our chances.</i>


00:31:02.161 --> 00:31:05.286
<i>If you're reading this,
that means I've either been crushed,</i>


00:31:05.455 --> 00:31:08.164
<i>impaled, pole-axed, harpooned,</i>


00:31:08.333 --> 00:31:10.875
<i>eaten alive by carnivorous beetles,</i>


00:31:11.045 --> 00:31:13.420
<i>drowned in a sea full of sharks,</i>


00:31:13.588 --> 00:31:17.255
<i>killed by birds
pecking at my every being.</i>


00:31:31.189 --> 00:31:32.855
So, so parched.


00:31:37.153 --> 00:31:38.361
Water?


00:31:40.365 --> 00:31:42.324
Oh, that goes down nice.
Oh yeah.


00:31:42.492 --> 00:31:43.701
So, parched.


00:31:44.453 --> 00:31:46.328
That jet stream gets me every time.


00:31:46.496 --> 00:31:47.580
Well?


00:31:47.747 --> 00:31:49.456
Huh? Oh, yeah uh…


00:31:49.624 --> 00:31:52.583
The King took the bait.
Everything's going like we planned.


00:31:52.752 --> 00:31:53.961
<i>Like we planned?</i>


00:31:54.421 --> 00:31:55.546
Well, yeah, okay.


00:31:55.714 --> 00:31:59.214
Technically it was your plan,
but I agreed it was a great plan.


00:31:59.968 --> 00:32:02.009
No, it's the perfect plan.


00:32:02.512 --> 00:32:05.304
- Well, not quite perfect.
- What?


00:32:06.057 --> 00:32:07.057
It's your nephew.


00:32:07.225 --> 00:32:08.225
The freak?


00:32:08.560 --> 00:32:10.602
He knows where the hamster is.


00:32:10.770 --> 00:32:14.187
And he and his little turtle friend
are following us.


00:32:14.357 --> 00:32:16.565
Hey, I figured we could wait for them,


00:32:16.735 --> 00:32:20.568
then flank them
and engage them in a nautical battle.


00:32:21.823 --> 00:32:23.865
I've always wanted
to be in a nautical battle.


00:32:24.200 --> 00:32:28.117
Please remember you're here
because of your wings, not your brain.


00:32:28.579 --> 00:32:30.912
I cannot waste valuable time
on the off chance


00:32:31.082 --> 00:32:34.040
that the freak actually makes it
across the ocean.


00:32:35.003 --> 00:32:36.128
No,


00:32:36.420 --> 00:32:38.920
we'll subcontract this one out.


00:32:39.423 --> 00:32:43.673
And I have just the animal
for the job.


00:32:46.389 --> 00:32:47.514
<i>Luther,</i>


00:32:47.681 --> 00:32:50.015
<i>the last member of our team.</i>


00:32:50.393 --> 00:32:52.351
<i>The most ruthless animal</i>


00:32:52.520 --> 00:32:54.770
<i>I've ever had the pleasure
of working with.</i>


00:32:54.939 --> 00:32:55.939
<i>He's so mean,</i>


00:32:56.690 --> 00:32:58.690
<i>he once killed an animal</i>


00:32:58.943 --> 00:33:00.610
<i>just for snoring.</i>


00:33:02.696 --> 00:33:05.488
I have sleep apnea.


00:33:06.492 --> 00:33:07.575
It's pretty bad.


00:33:07.743 --> 00:33:09.326
Can we get separate rooms?


00:33:10.288 --> 00:33:13.288
Lapin, it's been too long.


00:33:16.044 --> 00:33:17.835
It's okay, little guy…


00:33:38.857 --> 00:33:42.899
This city is where Alexander the Sweaty
discovered the Mustache of Destiny.


00:33:44.154 --> 00:33:46.237
Isn't this place great?


00:33:46.407 --> 00:33:50.032
Yeah. Great place to get murdered.
Why are we here anyway?


00:33:50.202 --> 00:33:51.368
Follow me.


00:33:53.372 --> 00:33:54.872
This very tavern


00:33:55.040 --> 00:33:58.332
is where Hector the Lost
hired the legless sherpa


00:33:58.502 --> 00:34:00.502
who led him to the Atheist's Temple.


00:34:00.921 --> 00:34:03.379
I never thought I'd see it
with my own eyes.


00:34:03.549 --> 00:34:06.257
I think you and I have
very different bucket lists.


00:34:09.722 --> 00:34:12.263
With any luck,
this is where we'll find our guide.


00:34:12.641 --> 00:34:14.641
Or at least a communicable disease.


00:34:14.810 --> 00:34:16.560
Hey. You need a guide?


00:34:17.020 --> 00:34:18.354
I'm your gal.


00:34:18.522 --> 00:34:21.397
I know that jungle
like the back of my tail. And the front.


00:34:21.567 --> 00:34:24.067
Don't do it, kid. She's bad news.


00:34:24.236 --> 00:34:26.736
Only a fool without a snout
would hire a skunk.


00:34:27.030 --> 00:34:28.905
The guy you want's over there.


00:34:35.455 --> 00:34:36.955
Excuse me?


00:34:37.374 --> 00:34:38.749
I'm looking for a guide.


00:34:39.292 --> 00:34:42.084
Well, fellow hare,


00:34:42.254 --> 00:34:43.879
you've come to the right rat.


00:34:44.047 --> 00:34:47.756
The name's Rusty,
but my sense of direction's not.


00:34:48.135 --> 00:34:51.760
Come on, let's go talk in the back,
away from prying ears.


00:34:51.930 --> 00:34:54.305
Yup.
I think we can totally trust this guy.


00:34:54.474 --> 00:34:56.266
Not suspicious at all.


00:35:01.857 --> 00:35:05.357
- So Rusty, we gotta go to…
- I already know where you're going.


00:35:05.861 --> 00:35:07.028
You do?


00:35:07.195 --> 00:35:09.737
Wow.
No wonder you're a guide.


00:35:10.282 --> 00:35:11.782
You're going with him.


00:35:17.414 --> 00:35:18.830
He's joking, right?


00:35:22.335 --> 00:35:25.585
Please tell me we've stumbled
into a very messed-up daycare.


00:35:26.339 --> 00:35:27.631
Rusty?


00:35:27.799 --> 00:35:28.965
Is this guide humor?


00:35:29.134 --> 00:35:33.217
You didn't tell me this guy was looking
for the Hamster of Darkness.


00:35:34.972 --> 00:35:36.764
You lose your manners
along with that eye?


00:35:37.475 --> 00:35:39.267
Stay out of this skunk!


00:35:39.644 --> 00:35:41.769
Yeah, it's me,
I'm Meg by the way.


00:35:41.938 --> 00:35:45.104
I don't care.
Now give me that map.


00:35:45.400 --> 00:35:48.067
Over our dead bodies.


00:35:48.236 --> 00:35:50.278
So, Mr. Gorilla, just to be clear,


00:35:50.447 --> 00:35:53.488
Meg was speaking metaphorically
about the dead bodies thing.


00:35:54.534 --> 00:35:55.742
He's a literalist.


00:36:05.462 --> 00:36:06.545
Take this!


00:36:06.713 --> 00:36:09.046
Yeah, my kind of girl!


00:36:13.886 --> 00:36:15.761
We're in a bar fight, Abe!


00:36:26.315 --> 00:36:27.857
Our map! He's getting away.


00:36:28.025 --> 00:36:29.359
Or not.


00:36:31.696 --> 00:36:34.696
Yeah, come on,
is that all you got?


00:36:47.378 --> 00:36:49.044
Meg, you're amazing.


00:36:49.546 --> 00:36:52.296
I'm assuming you're not going
with Rusty as your guide.


00:36:52.466 --> 00:36:54.633
You know,
because of the whole betrayal thing.


00:36:54.802 --> 00:36:56.177
You're hired!


00:36:56.595 --> 00:37:00.220
This should probably be a lesson,
don't judge a book by its cover,


00:37:00.391 --> 00:37:03.016
'cause you might end up
reading a really bad book.


00:37:10.734 --> 00:37:14.317
I'm really, really sorry.


00:37:14.488 --> 00:37:16.280
Meg? We've got a problem…


00:37:16.448 --> 00:37:18.157
And I've got the solution.


00:37:18.325 --> 00:37:19.909
Guys, put these on.


00:37:21.662 --> 00:37:22.787
Now.


00:37:31.088 --> 00:37:32.297
What a blast!


00:37:32.464 --> 00:37:34.923
I'm gonna keep this if that's okay.


00:37:38.054 --> 00:37:41.804
Oh darn,
I need to change your diaper.


00:37:46.395 --> 00:37:50.478
Hold up. This sweat is chaffing me
like there's no tomorrow…


00:37:50.649 --> 00:37:52.441
Which there probably isn't.


00:37:55.987 --> 00:37:57.279
That's better.


00:38:00.534 --> 00:38:03.201
A little hot in that jacket?


00:38:03.370 --> 00:38:06.745
Not at all.
I'm actually a little cold.


00:38:06.915 --> 00:38:10.082
Okay… So, I know
we haven't talked compensation,


00:38:10.251 --> 00:38:12.043
but I have a proposal.


00:38:12.212 --> 00:38:15.337
I'll take you to wherever
you wanna go for free.


00:38:15.757 --> 00:38:16.882
What's the catch?


00:38:17.050 --> 00:38:19.342
I've been on a fair number
of adventures myself,


00:38:19.511 --> 00:38:22.928
exclusively solo expeditions,
you know, 'cause of the skunk thing.


00:38:23.599 --> 00:38:26.890
And the truth is,
it's been kind of lonely.


00:38:32.733 --> 00:38:36.691
Meg, you can stay
with us as long as you like.


00:38:37.112 --> 00:38:38.237
- Really?
- Really?


00:38:38.404 --> 00:38:40.946
You are not going to regret this.
No sirree.


00:38:41.116 --> 00:38:44.324
I gotta say, I think we're on the cusp
of something great here.


00:38:44.494 --> 00:38:47.369
Something epic,
something unprecedented.


00:38:50.000 --> 00:38:53.083
Hamster of Darkness.
That's the Big One.


00:38:53.253 --> 00:38:55.878
When we find it,
they'll put us on the cover


00:38:56.047 --> 00:38:58.881
<i>of Adventure Weekly
and Adventure Monthly.</i>


00:39:00.761 --> 00:39:03.177
And Chickenhare,
if they put your name first,


00:39:03.346 --> 00:39:06.888
I'm totally fine with that,
just happy to be part of the team.


00:39:07.058 --> 00:39:09.683
You think she brought anything
to plug my ears?


00:39:11.521 --> 00:39:13.812
Hey, what kind of name
is Chickenhare anyway?


00:39:13.982 --> 00:39:15.774
Is that part Yukinarian?


00:39:16.484 --> 00:39:18.317
I actually don't know.


00:39:18.486 --> 00:39:22.236
Really? No clue?
Because it is such a unique name.


00:39:22.407 --> 00:39:24.490
Well, it's very unusual.


00:39:24.659 --> 00:39:27.409
Because I see the hare,
but I don't see the chicken.


00:39:27.578 --> 00:39:30.287
I'm gonna figure this out,
I'm great at puzzles.


00:39:37.588 --> 00:39:41.422
Well, that's too bad.
Looks like we'll have to head back.


00:39:42.635 --> 00:39:43.760
Follow me.


00:39:46.431 --> 00:39:47.597
Your turn.


00:39:49.225 --> 00:39:50.350
Why can't I meet anyone


00:39:50.518 --> 00:39:52.810
who shares my pessimism?


00:39:55.440 --> 00:39:59.440
If you take off that jacket,
it might help with your follow-through.


00:39:59.610 --> 00:40:02.527
Just a suggestion.
What do I know, I'm just a skunk, right?


00:40:02.905 --> 00:40:06.238
No, no. I'm good!
Third time's a charm!


00:40:10.162 --> 00:40:11.162
Now what?


00:40:13.416 --> 00:40:15.374
Stay put and don't try
anything foolish.


00:40:22.967 --> 00:40:26.008
I expected more from you, Luther.


00:40:26.178 --> 00:40:29.136
I won't tolerate another mistake.


00:40:29.306 --> 00:40:32.681
And why is this thing even here,


00:40:32.852 --> 00:40:36.352
why isn't he at home with your wife?
What has happened to you?


00:40:36.522 --> 00:40:39.189
See, Lapin,
me and my wife have 2-3 jobs.


00:40:39.358 --> 00:40:41.733
It's hard, you know,
providing for the baby.


00:40:41.902 --> 00:40:45.027
See, I can't afford
the cost of diapers and…


00:40:45.197 --> 00:40:46.197
Enough!


00:40:46.365 --> 00:40:50.865
Has the entire criminal underworld
gone soft since I've been locked up?


00:40:52.329 --> 00:40:56.037
Do me a favor,
go back to your wife.


00:40:56.709 --> 00:40:58.042
Go!


00:41:01.338 --> 00:41:03.171
Oh good, the duck's back.


00:41:03.716 --> 00:41:05.841
Please tell me
something positive.


00:41:06.093 --> 00:41:08.468
Chickenhare made it through
the Desert of Death.


00:41:08.888 --> 00:41:10.471
What? Impossible!


00:41:10.806 --> 00:41:14.098
Well, technically improbable
since he did make it through.


00:41:14.268 --> 00:41:15.934
He's just a couple clicks behind us.


00:41:16.353 --> 00:41:17.603
What are clicks?


00:41:17.772 --> 00:41:21.730
I hear that term on missions like this,
but I don't know what they are.


00:41:21.901 --> 00:41:23.817
Destroy the bridge.


00:41:23.986 --> 00:41:26.653
It will take them a week
to get around the quicksand.


00:41:27.865 --> 00:41:32.323
By then, I'll have Featherbeard
completely under my control.


00:41:33.287 --> 00:41:35.620
Our control.


00:41:36.957 --> 00:41:39.291
Your control… obviously.


00:41:52.306 --> 00:41:55.681
We'll have to go around,
that's gonna take at least a week.


00:41:55.850 --> 00:41:57.309
We don't have a week.


00:41:57.477 --> 00:42:00.394
My Uncle Lapin'll already have
the hamster by then.


00:42:00.564 --> 00:42:01.605
We can cross it.


00:42:02.149 --> 00:42:05.232
Sure, for a couple of feet.
But then we'd die!


00:42:05.819 --> 00:42:09.360
Because this is quicksand!
Quicksand sucks you under until you die!


00:42:09.531 --> 00:42:11.989
That's what it does!
That's its reason for existing!


00:42:12.159 --> 00:42:16.409
Chickenhare is right, we should try.
The quicksand is only in a few spots.


00:42:16.580 --> 00:42:18.996
If we avoid those spots,
we'll have a solid path.


00:42:19.666 --> 00:42:21.416
Do you know where that path is?


00:42:21.585 --> 00:42:23.751
Just follow in my footsteps
and you'll be okay.


00:42:25.171 --> 00:42:26.546
I'll go last.


00:42:30.385 --> 00:42:32.135
Who's this Uncle Lapin?


00:42:32.804 --> 00:42:34.637
He's just a genius adventurer


00:42:34.806 --> 00:42:40.056
with grandiose plans most likely
covering a deep-seeded insecurity.


00:42:40.228 --> 00:42:43.019
Sounds like someone else I know.


00:42:43.898 --> 00:42:45.648
- Chickenhare!
- Oh no!


00:42:45.817 --> 00:42:47.692
- Chickenhare!
- Abe, help!


00:42:48.069 --> 00:42:51.236
Grab onto me.
Darn, I'm a goner too.


00:42:51.405 --> 00:42:52.655
Hey, watch the shell!


00:42:52.824 --> 00:42:54.449
Hold on, Chickenhare.


00:42:58.663 --> 00:42:59.663
Meg!


00:42:59.831 --> 00:43:01.248
I'm going down!


00:43:01.415 --> 00:43:03.165
Stay still, don't move.


00:43:12.761 --> 00:43:13.969
What are you doing?


00:43:14.137 --> 00:43:15.595
Grab the whip!


00:43:16.014 --> 00:43:18.389
With your hands!
Isn't that kind of implied?


00:43:20.018 --> 00:43:21.018
Just pull!


00:43:22.645 --> 00:43:24.770
A little help, Abe!
Hurry!


00:43:27.608 --> 00:43:28.733
You need to use your hands!


00:43:29.277 --> 00:43:32.443
Isn't it a pretty simple concept
he's failing to grasp? Abe!


00:43:43.124 --> 00:43:45.832
Oh, my gosh!
I'm pulling him out of his skin!


00:43:54.927 --> 00:43:57.635
Wait, are those… chicken legs?


00:43:59.848 --> 00:44:03.182
Hold on a second.
Chickenhare… Oh, lightning bolt!


00:44:03.352 --> 00:44:05.519
That's where the name
comes from!


00:44:05.688 --> 00:44:08.729
Told you I was great at puzzles!
Those are chicken feet.


00:44:09.567 --> 00:44:12.358
You're part chicken, part hare,
aren't you?


00:44:14.488 --> 00:44:16.822
Hello, what about me?


00:44:16.990 --> 00:44:20.199
Hey, a little help here, guys,
I'm stuck.


00:44:26.959 --> 00:44:29.042
- Do you have other chicken parts?
- No.


00:44:33.173 --> 00:44:34.173
Hey!


00:44:34.550 --> 00:44:35.967
That is… awesome!


00:44:36.844 --> 00:44:39.302
What else?
Do you have wings?


00:44:39.972 --> 00:44:41.680
You have wings under that jacket!


00:44:41.849 --> 00:44:45.724
Nope. You've seen the top-shelf stuff.
He has a couple feathers under there.


00:44:45.894 --> 00:44:47.936
- Lemme see 'em.
- No!


00:44:48.356 --> 00:44:51.106
- Are there other chickenhares?
- Not that I know of.


00:44:51.274 --> 00:44:54.483
You're your own species!
How awesome is that?


00:44:54.653 --> 00:44:56.612
You're basically
automatically endangered.


00:44:56.780 --> 00:44:59.614
- It's not awesome!
- So like what you can do?


00:44:59.783 --> 00:45:01.533
Oh my gosh, you can fly!


00:45:01.702 --> 00:45:04.577
I can't fly.
Chickens can't even fly.


00:45:04.747 --> 00:45:07.247
Technically they can over
very short distances.


00:45:07.415 --> 00:45:09.790
Oh come on,
but you're only part chicken.


00:45:09.960 --> 00:45:12.085
How many flying hares
have you ever seen?


00:45:12.588 --> 00:45:14.171
Well, none.


00:45:14.339 --> 00:45:17.964
But I've also never seen a hare
with such gigantic floppy ears.


00:45:18.135 --> 00:45:21.051
- I mean, on an elephant.
- I can't fly!


00:45:22.180 --> 00:45:24.264
You can fly!


00:45:29.646 --> 00:45:31.687
See, I can't fly.


00:45:32.232 --> 00:45:34.857
I can't clear a bar
with my scent like you Meg.


00:45:35.318 --> 00:45:38.568
There's nothing good
about being me, okay?


00:45:39.281 --> 00:45:41.739
You've got a "me" problem.


00:45:44.995 --> 00:45:47.245
I think we got a "we" problem.


00:45:48.498 --> 00:45:49.498
Oh no!


00:46:32.959 --> 00:46:34.292
Pigmies?


00:46:37.714 --> 00:46:40.297
Heya! We come in peace.


00:46:40.467 --> 00:46:42.717
For the record,
I didn't wanna come at all.


00:46:42.885 --> 00:46:44.344
Blast 'em. Blast 'em all.


00:46:44.512 --> 00:46:47.096
Hold on, I can't,
I haven't recharged yet.


00:46:47.264 --> 00:46:50.181
"Haven't recharged!"
What happened to being special?


00:46:54.814 --> 00:46:57.231
Hey! That tickles!


00:46:58.860 --> 00:47:00.193
Behold!


00:47:00.945 --> 00:47:02.237
The Chickenhare!


00:47:02.405 --> 00:47:04.697
God of the land and sky!


00:47:04.991 --> 00:47:07.449
Flyer over short distances!


00:47:08.244 --> 00:47:10.619
Part chicken, part hare.


00:47:10.788 --> 00:47:12.372
Almighty!


00:47:29.056 --> 00:47:32.056
You are a god?


00:47:33.728 --> 00:47:34.811
Sure?


00:47:35.354 --> 00:47:37.354
That's good enough for me.


00:47:37.523 --> 00:47:39.773
Prepare the feast!


00:47:40.401 --> 00:47:41.859
See, "me" problem.


00:47:42.028 --> 00:47:43.111
Tonight,


00:47:43.279 --> 00:47:46.904
we shall ply
the almighty Chickenhare


00:47:47.074 --> 00:47:49.658
and his strange helpers


00:47:49.827 --> 00:47:52.702
with our finest banquet!


00:47:54.040 --> 00:47:57.665
And then, tomorrow at first light,


00:47:57.835 --> 00:48:00.210
we shall take them to our volcano,


00:48:01.380 --> 00:48:04.588
and sacrifice the god Chickenhare


00:48:04.841 --> 00:48:08.883
to our god…
Santoro the Stoic!


00:48:09.055 --> 00:48:11.305
I think you're just the thing


00:48:11.473 --> 00:48:16.265
to finally put a smile
on Santoro's face.


00:48:16.437 --> 00:48:17.687
Just to be clear,


00:48:18.272 --> 00:48:21.397
Chickenhare's the only one
going in the volcano, right?


00:48:35.747 --> 00:48:37.289
That meal was incredible.


00:48:37.458 --> 00:48:39.499
These guys know how
to throw a sacrifice.


00:48:39.918 --> 00:48:43.668
See, Meg, this is what happens
when I'm myself.


00:48:43.839 --> 00:48:46.380
Maybe we could take a break
from the pity party?


00:48:46.550 --> 00:48:49.092
Let me tell you
about a little skunk named…


00:48:49.261 --> 00:48:50.886
I don't know… "Peg."


00:48:51.430 --> 00:48:55.430
I love a good story,
especially after a meal like that.


00:48:55.767 --> 00:48:58.517
Growing up, nobody wanted
to have a play date with "Peg,"


00:48:58.687 --> 00:49:00.479
on account of her being a skunk.


00:49:00.647 --> 00:49:04.772
Even when she got cool new dolls,
and had goody bags for her birthday,


00:49:04.943 --> 00:49:06.610
<i>nobody came.</i>


00:49:06.778 --> 00:49:09.070
<i>She bathed twice a day,
didn't matter.</i>


00:49:09.239 --> 00:49:11.947
<i>So… she corked herself.</i>


00:49:12.117 --> 00:49:13.783
Ouch!


00:49:14.119 --> 00:49:15.702
Ouch is right.


00:49:16.121 --> 00:49:17.704
But that didn't work either.


00:49:17.873 --> 00:49:20.831
So naturally, "Peg" got angry…


00:49:21.001 --> 00:49:23.959
<i>Her parents wanted her anger channeled
into something positive.</i>


00:49:24.129 --> 00:49:26.337
<i>So, she got a black belt in karate…</i>


00:49:26.507 --> 00:49:27.923
<i>and Kung Fu…</i>


00:49:28.091 --> 00:49:29.508
<i>and Kendo…</i>


00:49:29.926 --> 00:49:31.801
<i>and seven other martial arts.</i>


00:49:31.970 --> 00:49:35.387
<i>But that didn't help either.
She was still angry.</i>


00:49:35.807 --> 00:49:39.682
<i>Deep down, "Peg" still wished
she was anything but a skunk.</i>


00:49:40.020 --> 00:49:43.436
<i>Until one day, when she went
on a field trip to the Royal Treasury,</i>


00:49:44.232 --> 00:49:48.940
<i>and then Billy Goat Jones,
the jerk who teased "Peg" the most,</i>


00:49:49.570 --> 00:49:51.279
<i>shut the door behind us.</i>


00:49:51.698 --> 00:49:54.448
<i>But the treasurer was
the only one with the combination.</i>


00:49:54.910 --> 00:49:57.160
<i>Know what happens
when a skunk fears for her life?</i>


00:49:57.328 --> 00:50:00.203
<i>Well, "Peg" was a skunk
who feared for her life</i>


00:50:00.373 --> 00:50:02.331
<i>and had been corked for 3 years.</i>


00:50:05.211 --> 00:50:07.170
<i>"Peg" saved everyone that day.</i>


00:50:07.338 --> 00:50:10.255
<i>And you were a big hero
and everyone loved you, Meg.</i>


00:50:11.509 --> 00:50:12.717
<i>I mean "Peg".</i>


00:50:12.886 --> 00:50:15.886
<i>No, they treated me worse than ever.</i>


00:50:16.056 --> 00:50:18.931
But for the first time,
I didn't care.


00:50:19.100 --> 00:50:23.309
I realized the thing that I was corking,
wasn't something to be ashamed of.


00:50:23.479 --> 00:50:25.688
No, it's what made me special.


00:50:26.232 --> 00:50:28.899
Chickenhare, you're a corker.


00:50:29.069 --> 00:50:33.444
Until you blow open your treasury vault,
you won't know what makes you special.


00:50:34.907 --> 00:50:36.240
Nice story, Meg,


00:50:36.409 --> 00:50:38.409
and I liked the way
you changed your name


00:50:38.578 --> 00:50:40.494
to make it feel more universal.


00:50:40.663 --> 00:50:42.830
But when the volcano turns us to ash,


00:50:42.998 --> 00:50:46.707
it isn't gonna discriminate
between the corkers and the non-corkers.


00:50:46.877 --> 00:50:50.086
True. But they're not gonna
throw us in that volcano.


00:50:51.507 --> 00:50:53.591
- They're not?
- Nope.


00:50:53.759 --> 00:50:55.676
Because you're gonna break us out.


00:51:01.559 --> 00:51:04.226
- Are you sure about this?
- Trust me.


00:51:53.318 --> 00:51:54.318
Chickenhare.


00:52:01.118 --> 00:52:02.701
I'll be right back.


00:52:03.287 --> 00:52:04.287
No.


00:52:10.669 --> 00:52:11.669
Really?


00:52:23.390 --> 00:52:25.515
Chickenhare, don't.


00:52:31.148 --> 00:52:32.981
You don't need those.


00:53:17.402 --> 00:53:18.861
Well, you know,


00:53:19.028 --> 00:53:23.445
I always felt waiting
'til first light was a bit arbitrary.


00:53:23.658 --> 00:53:25.408
Take them to the volcano now!


00:53:25.577 --> 00:53:26.744
Put down your weapons,


00:53:26.911 --> 00:53:28.786
or your god gets it!


00:53:29.706 --> 00:53:30.706
Abe?


00:53:31.416 --> 00:53:33.041
Come on, guys, hurry up.


00:53:34.335 --> 00:53:37.335
Look how Santoro maintains his stoicism,


00:53:37.922 --> 00:53:40.881
even with a spear at his throat.


00:53:41.050 --> 00:53:45.300
Let's see how he maintains
his stoicism rolling down a hill!


00:53:45.639 --> 00:53:48.555
Now they'll all follow him
as we make our escape…


00:53:53.437 --> 00:53:55.729
- Or not.
- Get them!


00:53:59.819 --> 00:54:01.486
Oh great Santoro,


00:54:01.655 --> 00:54:04.780
your revenge is at hand!


00:54:11.622 --> 00:54:12.872
Watch out!


00:54:14.208 --> 00:54:16.792
This is not worth
perpetual three-day weekends!


00:54:19.839 --> 00:54:20.839
No, come here!


00:54:44.488 --> 00:54:47.113
- Please tell me you've recharged!
- I'm trying!


00:54:47.283 --> 00:54:48.783
Almost there.


00:54:54.248 --> 00:54:56.790
I'm really starting to think
you're not special at all,


00:54:56.959 --> 00:54:58.334
you just have an enormous ego!


00:54:58.627 --> 00:55:00.502
There we go, I'm back.


00:55:00.671 --> 00:55:01.879
Fire in the hole!


00:55:13.642 --> 00:55:15.017
Chickenhare!


00:55:28.741 --> 00:55:31.199
- Chickenhare! This way!
- Coming!


00:55:48.844 --> 00:55:50.969
Chickenhare!
Your moves have moves.


00:56:07.738 --> 00:56:09.321
Good work, Chickenhare.


00:56:09.489 --> 00:56:10.489
Did you see that?


00:56:15.453 --> 00:56:16.453
Let's go.


00:56:19.875 --> 00:56:20.917
Look!


00:56:21.084 --> 00:56:23.584
Woah, the mountain!


00:56:32.762 --> 00:56:34.304
Incoming!


00:56:39.144 --> 00:56:41.519
- Meg, get us across!
- I can't do it.


00:56:42.022 --> 00:56:43.772
I can't do it.
Last time I tried…


00:56:43.941 --> 00:56:46.524
Last time your jacket
was holding your arm back.


00:56:48.028 --> 00:56:49.486
You're almost here, Chickenhare.


00:56:53.908 --> 00:56:56.116
- I did it! Hang on!
- Here we go!


00:57:00.248 --> 00:57:01.248
Oh, please.


00:57:01.791 --> 00:57:03.166
No!


00:57:05.253 --> 00:57:07.420
You couldn't have brought
the extra-large whip,


00:57:07.589 --> 00:57:08.922
could you, Meg?


00:57:10.425 --> 00:57:11.800
I hate adventuring!


00:57:15.722 --> 00:57:17.805
Hey! It's even further than I thought.


00:57:36.909 --> 00:57:40.284
According to the map,
the temple's at the top of the mountain.


00:57:40.455 --> 00:57:41.455
We need a plan.


00:57:41.623 --> 00:57:43.873
Lapin is probably
halfway up there already.


00:57:44.041 --> 00:57:45.083
I have a plan!


00:57:45.418 --> 00:57:47.460
If we take the Nearly Impassable Pass,


00:57:47.920 --> 00:57:51.045
by the time the trails merge,
we should be ahead of them…


00:57:51.215 --> 00:57:53.048
Sounds like a genius plan to me.


00:57:53.217 --> 00:57:56.259
You know what? We might get
that Hamster of Darkness after all.


00:57:56.429 --> 00:58:00.679
What do you mean "might"?
Lapin's gonna eat our feather dust.


00:58:02.059 --> 00:58:03.059
Abe?


00:58:04.854 --> 00:58:06.854
This mud is actually very nutrient-rich.


00:58:07.439 --> 00:58:08.898
Uh, let's go.


00:58:09.066 --> 00:58:11.941
Hey, I wanna stop Lapin
as much as you,


00:58:12.111 --> 00:58:13.944
well maybe 10% as much as you,


00:58:14.113 --> 00:58:16.405
but can't we look good doing it?


00:58:37.428 --> 00:58:39.469
Here I am. You won't believe it.


00:58:39.638 --> 00:58:42.888
Chickenhare's heading up
the Nearly Impassable Pass!


00:58:43.059 --> 00:58:44.642
What? Impossible!


00:58:44.977 --> 00:58:48.394
No, again I think
it's more improbable than impossible.


00:58:48.564 --> 00:58:51.064
You know, I tell you what,
the way he's going,


00:58:51.567 --> 00:58:55.067
the Three Deadly Trials
won't be a problem for Chickenhare.


00:58:59.992 --> 00:59:01.909
Get the dynamite.


00:59:02.744 --> 00:59:03.869
Come on, Abe!


00:59:04.955 --> 00:59:06.496
We're closing in on them.


00:59:06.790 --> 00:59:08.040
Hello, I'm a turtle!


00:59:08.209 --> 00:59:11.917
Are you completely unaware
of my species' role in fables?


00:59:18.594 --> 00:59:19.594
You idiots!


00:59:19.761 --> 00:59:23.636
The avalanche was supposed
to take out Chickenhare, not us!


00:59:28.562 --> 00:59:31.270
It really is difficult
to find good help these days.


00:59:33.192 --> 00:59:34.275
Lapin!


00:59:34.776 --> 00:59:36.110
Lapin!


00:59:36.278 --> 00:59:37.903
Look, Lapin's a goner.


00:59:40.115 --> 00:59:42.198
I guess there's nothing we can do.


00:59:42.368 --> 00:59:43.368
Yeah there is.


00:59:47.331 --> 00:59:48.873
You're right,
nothing we can do.


00:59:49.040 --> 00:59:50.290
Oh, let's go.


00:59:50.459 --> 00:59:51.876
Sorry, guys.


01:00:03.847 --> 01:00:05.555
According to the legend,


01:00:05.724 --> 01:00:09.516
we're looking for a hamster face
etched in the ice.


01:00:24.200 --> 01:00:25.450
I got it!


01:00:26.870 --> 01:00:28.078
This way!


01:00:37.839 --> 01:00:39.839
Alright, we're going in.


01:00:40.008 --> 01:00:41.716
You read my mind, partner.


01:00:41.927 --> 01:00:44.468
Wait. Lapin's dead and buried.


01:00:44.637 --> 01:00:46.345
Probably not in that order.


01:00:46.514 --> 01:00:49.306
We saved the Kingdom.
We're done here. Let's go home.


01:00:49.475 --> 01:00:52.809
Abe, if I can bring back
the Hamster of Darkness,


01:00:52.979 --> 01:00:55.688
my dad will let me join
the Royal Adventure Society.


01:00:56.066 --> 01:00:58.107
Isn't it enough
that you made it this far?


01:00:58.276 --> 01:01:00.068
And who's gonna believe me?


01:01:00.236 --> 01:01:02.695
I need the hamster as proof.


01:01:02.863 --> 01:01:05.572
Now the only thing
standing between us and it


01:01:05.741 --> 01:01:07.575
are the Three Deadly Trials.


01:01:07.743 --> 01:01:09.993
Abe, if you wanna stay behind,
fine, but…


01:01:10.413 --> 01:01:11.663
I'm in!


01:01:17.087 --> 01:01:19.128
I've always been a follower.


01:01:19.672 --> 01:01:22.547
I want every other Thursday off too!


01:01:28.264 --> 01:01:31.723
"In order to enter
the Temple of the Hamster of Darkness,


01:01:31.892 --> 01:01:34.809
"one must pass the Three Deadly Trials."


01:01:34.979 --> 01:01:38.937
Why's it always three?
Why can't it ever be two trials?


01:01:42.278 --> 01:01:43.612
What's the first one?


01:01:43.779 --> 01:01:46.321
"We hamsters may be small of stature,


01:01:46.491 --> 01:01:48.449
"but we are cool under pressure.


01:01:48.618 --> 01:01:49.826
"We never lose our heads,


01:01:51.954 --> 01:01:55.162
"even when confronted
by imminent death."


01:01:55.333 --> 01:01:58.083
"Imminent death!"
That's how we start?


01:02:01.881 --> 01:02:03.964
Sadistic little rodents, aren't they?


01:02:10.515 --> 01:02:11.973
"Small of stature"…


01:02:18.188 --> 01:02:19.480
"Cool under pressure"…


01:02:31.368 --> 01:02:32.451
A secret passage!


01:02:32.912 --> 01:02:34.912
- Well done!
- Let's get out of here!


01:02:47.885 --> 01:02:49.677
What's the second trial?


01:02:50.345 --> 01:02:54.887
"Though we hamsters may not be so fleet
of foot to outrun our Destiny,


01:02:55.267 --> 01:02:57.684
"we do have the courage to face it."


01:02:58.270 --> 01:03:00.770
Enough with this fake
self-deprecating routine.


01:03:00.940 --> 01:03:03.690
Why couldn't these hamsters
hire shrinks like us?


01:03:10.574 --> 01:03:12.115
Run!


01:03:19.166 --> 01:03:21.166
Look, that's Ramon's wife!


01:03:21.335 --> 01:03:24.335
It's wonderful that you're an admirer
of the female form…


01:03:25.005 --> 01:03:27.797
His wife Destiny.
We have to stand here facing Destiny.


01:03:28.758 --> 01:03:30.258
Or… we can run!


01:03:30.427 --> 01:03:33.302
Meg, if you're gonna side with me
once before I die,


01:03:33.472 --> 01:03:35.138
you have 10 seconds.
9…


01:03:35.307 --> 01:03:36.307
I'm with Chickenhare.


01:03:38.435 --> 01:03:40.643
Miscalculated!
7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1…


01:04:19.934 --> 01:04:22.518
Think these hamsters
had issues with being short?


01:04:22.854 --> 01:04:25.604
Do I even wanna ask
what the third trial is?


01:04:25.899 --> 01:04:28.190
All the legend says, is:
"Do this."


01:04:28.359 --> 01:04:29.359
Do what?


01:04:39.453 --> 01:04:41.620
That can't be it. Could it?


01:05:19.493 --> 01:05:22.077
Man, these hamsters
keep you off-balance.


01:05:33.591 --> 01:05:34.966
The scepter…


01:05:38.012 --> 01:05:39.012
We made it!


01:05:52.526 --> 01:05:54.610
I'm taking you home.


01:06:05.998 --> 01:06:08.748
The Hamster of Darkness.


01:06:11.337 --> 01:06:14.545
- But you…
- Were buried in that avalanche?


01:06:14.715 --> 01:06:17.382
Or did I make you think I was?


01:06:17.843 --> 01:06:20.468
See, I asked myself:


01:06:20.638 --> 01:06:23.846
Why should I try to pass
the Three Deadly Trials


01:06:24.016 --> 01:06:27.307
when my very eager nephew
would do it for me?


01:06:28.311 --> 01:06:29.520
Now give me that scepter.


01:06:29.688 --> 01:06:31.272
Don't do it. Don't give it to him!


01:06:32.149 --> 01:06:35.232
You're smart, Chickenhare.
I could use someone like you.


01:06:35.778 --> 01:06:39.403
You could be in charge
of my adventure society.


01:06:39.782 --> 01:06:41.823
We'll show everyone who laughs at us,


01:06:41.992 --> 01:06:45.659
take our revenge on those who'd shun us
because we're different.


01:06:45.829 --> 01:06:48.163
We're so alike, you and I.


01:06:48.999 --> 01:06:50.957
I'm nothing like you.


01:06:51.126 --> 01:06:54.043
But you are.
Because Chickenhare…


01:06:54.212 --> 01:06:55.504
I'm your father.


01:06:57.174 --> 01:06:59.049
I'm just kidding.
I'm not your father!


01:06:59.217 --> 01:07:01.509
But wouldn't it
have been crazy if I was,


01:07:01.679 --> 01:07:02.929
right?


01:07:04.139 --> 01:07:05.222
Give me that scepter or…


01:07:05.390 --> 01:07:08.140
One more step
and I'll throw it over the edge.


01:07:08.643 --> 01:07:10.935
Do it and I'll throw your friends over.


01:07:11.479 --> 01:07:12.979
Give it to him! Post haste.


01:07:13.315 --> 01:07:14.773
Do not call his bluff.


01:07:15.025 --> 01:07:17.358
Prisoners play a lot of poker!
A lot!


01:07:17.527 --> 01:07:20.360
If I give it to you,
you'll let them go?


01:07:20.697 --> 01:07:22.780
I'll let you all go.


01:07:22.950 --> 01:07:23.991
I swear it.


01:07:24.326 --> 01:07:26.326
Chickenhare, no, he's lying.


01:07:26.828 --> 01:07:29.994
Do you know the final piece
of the legend, Chickenhare?


01:07:31.416 --> 01:07:33.416
"He who releases the Hamster of Darkness


01:07:34.502 --> 01:07:37.002
"shall be followed for all of his days."


01:07:40.342 --> 01:07:42.550
That's right, little freak.


01:07:51.269 --> 01:07:53.644
I, Lapin the IX,


01:07:53.813 --> 01:07:55.563
call upon you


01:07:55.898 --> 01:07:58.315
to bring the darkness.


01:08:16.336 --> 01:08:17.794
What have I done?


01:08:24.636 --> 01:08:27.177
Now what do you say
we go take back my kingdom?


01:08:27.389 --> 01:08:31.639
- What about the freak and his friends?
- I promised I'd let them go.


01:08:31.809 --> 01:08:33.934
So, let them go… over the edge.


01:08:34.479 --> 01:08:35.937
Darn semantics…


01:08:43.613 --> 01:08:46.446
I have good news and bad news.


01:08:46.949 --> 01:08:49.158
The bad news is that
you should freeze to death


01:08:49.326 --> 01:08:51.743
in about 12 hours.


01:08:51.913 --> 01:08:54.121
Really? I think
it's gonna be much quicker.


01:08:54.290 --> 01:08:55.540
What's the good news?


01:08:55.708 --> 01:08:58.958
Please be that they're sending
a rope down for us.


01:08:59.128 --> 01:09:02.586
The good news is you'll live longer
than your father, Chickenhare.


01:09:03.299 --> 01:09:04.924
I wouldn't call that good news.


01:09:05.092 --> 01:09:07.134
Maybe slightly better news…


01:09:15.019 --> 01:09:16.519
We found nothing.


01:09:16.688 --> 01:09:19.271
It was just another
of my brother's tricks.


01:09:19.440 --> 01:09:21.440
Hope for the best
and prepare for the worst.


01:09:21.608 --> 01:09:24.192
If Lapin got to the scepter,
things could get rough.


01:09:24.486 --> 01:09:27.195
Go and take shelter in the dungeon.


01:09:30.784 --> 01:09:33.326
<i>Dad, I've gone to stop Lapin.</i>


01:09:33.495 --> 01:09:36.704
<i>I know I'm not an Adventurer like you,
but I'll try my best.</i>


01:09:36.874 --> 01:09:38.458
<i>I'm sorry for all this.</i>


01:09:38.625 --> 01:09:41.167
<i>I love you, Chickenhare.</i>


01:09:47.384 --> 01:09:48.593
This is all my fault.


01:09:48.760 --> 01:09:52.927
You know what? You're right!
It is all your fault! 100%!


01:09:53.182 --> 01:09:55.349
We could've gone home now, but no,


01:09:55.517 --> 01:09:57.434
you needed to find
the Hamster of Darkness.


01:09:57.603 --> 01:10:00.228
- So everyone would forget you're…
- A freak?


01:10:01.482 --> 01:10:04.815
I thought bringing it back
would make them accept me.


01:10:06.403 --> 01:10:08.028
It's not all your fault.


01:10:08.197 --> 01:10:10.530
It's Meg's fault too.
She's a terrible influence.


01:10:10.907 --> 01:10:14.116
And I wasn't gonna say "freak."
I was gonna say "Chickenhare."


01:10:14.578 --> 01:10:16.411
- Same thing.
- No, they're not.


01:10:16.830 --> 01:10:19.955
Look at me!
Why couldn't I just be normal?


01:10:20.125 --> 01:10:23.500
Lapin never would've escaped,
and I wouldn't've come all this way.


01:10:23.920 --> 01:10:27.587
Because you're not normal!
Pretending you were only made it worse.


01:10:28.133 --> 01:10:31.008
But when you got rid of that costume
and became you…


01:10:31.387 --> 01:10:32.803
You found the Hamster of Darkness.


01:10:32.971 --> 01:10:36.346
The treasure that no adventurer
could find for thousands of years.


01:10:36.642 --> 01:10:38.975
Yeah, Lapin never would've found it
without you.


01:10:39.144 --> 01:10:41.185
I'm trying to let it go,
but I can't.


01:10:41.355 --> 01:10:44.105
Look, all of us are born with things
that make us different.


01:10:44.274 --> 01:10:46.899
The only choice we have
is how we see those things.


01:10:47.193 --> 01:10:51.068
So, we can either be ashamed of them
or we can embrace them


01:10:51.239 --> 01:10:52.989
and recognize that our differences
make us…


01:10:53.158 --> 01:10:54.366
Special.


01:10:57.078 --> 01:10:58.578
- No!
- Chickenhare!


01:11:27.608 --> 01:11:28.608
Really?


01:11:35.700 --> 01:11:37.158
Come on, Abe.


01:11:38.369 --> 01:11:39.786
They're too far ahead.


01:11:39.955 --> 01:11:42.288
By the time we get to your kingdom,
it'll be too late.


01:11:42.623 --> 01:11:45.623
We've come too far.
There's gotta be a way.


01:11:45.793 --> 01:11:48.001
- I have a plan.
- You have a plan?


01:11:48.171 --> 01:11:50.213
I have my moments.


01:11:50.590 --> 01:11:52.090
My secret shame.


01:11:52.258 --> 01:11:54.175
I was born without a shell.


01:11:54.344 --> 01:11:57.719
This one's my Uncle Herb's…
Love you Uncle Herbie!


01:12:00.891 --> 01:12:04.058
What? It's not like I got feathers
growing out of my head.


01:12:04.229 --> 01:12:05.645
It's not that.


01:12:05.813 --> 01:12:07.771
It's just that…


01:12:08.066 --> 01:12:10.566
you're really pale.


01:12:11.319 --> 01:12:12.944
That is unattractive.


01:12:13.446 --> 01:12:15.613
Anyway, who's ready to ride?


01:12:19.577 --> 01:12:21.952
- Should've used less wax!
- Get down!


01:12:24.081 --> 01:12:25.081
Watch out!


01:12:34.259 --> 01:12:35.467
Alright!


01:12:35.635 --> 01:12:37.885
- We're gonna catch Lapin.
- Or not.


01:12:42.600 --> 01:12:44.350
I hate adventuring.


01:12:50.274 --> 01:12:52.024
Sir, Lapin's at the gate.


01:12:52.317 --> 01:12:54.276
He requests to see you.


01:12:54.987 --> 01:12:56.654
Let's settle this!


01:13:02.953 --> 01:13:06.745
Not another step forward, Brother,
until you tell me where my son is.


01:13:08.083 --> 01:13:10.958
You mean that worthless
little half-breed freak?


01:13:11.128 --> 01:13:13.045
He's not coming back.


01:13:13.213 --> 01:13:15.380
I made quite sure of that.


01:13:17.301 --> 01:13:18.467
Hold it.


01:13:18.636 --> 01:13:21.761
Brother, please. Where is my son?


01:13:23.974 --> 01:13:26.016
I assume by now he's frozen to death


01:13:26.185 --> 01:13:27.768
on the side of the cliff
I threw him over.


01:13:27.937 --> 01:13:28.937
No!


01:13:29.521 --> 01:13:30.521
The scepter?


01:13:30.898 --> 01:13:33.273
That's right! I found it.


01:13:34.068 --> 01:13:36.026
Ah, technically Chickenhare found…


01:13:36.195 --> 01:13:38.736
Enough talk. Hamsters, attack!


01:14:00.302 --> 01:14:02.094
Sounds like a lost cause.


01:14:02.262 --> 01:14:03.929
My favorite kind.


01:14:04.098 --> 01:14:05.889
Meg, I'll need your whip.


01:14:06.058 --> 01:14:07.350
Thought you'd never ask.


01:14:18.820 --> 01:14:20.487
We can sneak up on Lapin.


01:14:20.655 --> 01:14:23.739
That's a terrible plan,
he's got a million hamsters.


01:14:23.908 --> 01:14:24.950
Lance, Whitey!


01:14:25.119 --> 01:14:26.952
Chickenhare!
We thought you were dead.


01:14:27.121 --> 01:14:29.954
Nope. Alive and kicking with these.


01:14:30.124 --> 01:14:32.082
So, where do we stand?


01:14:32.834 --> 01:14:34.876
It looks pretty hopeless.


01:14:35.044 --> 01:14:36.169
We gotta get down there.


01:14:36.338 --> 01:14:39.505
We gotta figure out a way
to get past those million hamsters.


01:14:39.674 --> 01:14:40.966
With big tails.


01:14:41.510 --> 01:14:43.801
What? I was born without a shell.


01:14:44.137 --> 01:14:47.095
A dose of skepticism
has been essential to my survival.


01:14:48.057 --> 01:14:49.932
That's how we sneak up on Lapin!


01:14:50.101 --> 01:14:54.226
- With my skepticism?
- No, with your shell.


01:14:54.398 --> 01:14:58.023
Well, at least we know your plan's
not the worst one, Whitey.


01:14:59.027 --> 01:15:01.027
Mine, at long last.


01:15:03.823 --> 01:15:05.282
Perfect fit.


01:15:05.909 --> 01:15:08.909
Actually, I'll need
to have it taken in a little


01:15:09.078 --> 01:15:12.620
because you have
such a big fat head, Brother.


01:15:13.082 --> 01:15:14.999
Maybe you're not so perfect
after all.


01:15:20.381 --> 01:15:21.381
What?


01:15:21.550 --> 01:15:24.425
Peg, say hello
to my little smelly friend!


01:15:30.391 --> 01:15:32.141
Hey, Chickenhare's plan worked!


01:15:37.899 --> 01:15:39.066
Chickenhare!


01:15:40.026 --> 01:15:41.026
You?


01:15:41.194 --> 01:15:45.902
Hamsters, I command you to fight no more
and return to the scepter.


01:15:48.242 --> 01:15:49.659
I mean it.


01:15:49.828 --> 01:15:50.828
I'm serious.


01:15:51.204 --> 01:15:53.120
I command you!


01:15:54.082 --> 01:15:55.373
Please…


01:15:57.626 --> 01:15:58.835
Fool!


01:15:59.003 --> 01:16:01.670
That scepter is nothing without me.


01:16:02.048 --> 01:16:04.340
"For he who releases
the Hamster of Darkness


01:16:04.508 --> 01:16:07.258
"shall be followed for all of his days."


01:16:07.428 --> 01:16:08.845
The power's already mine.


01:16:09.013 --> 01:16:11.222
That's not true. Without the scepter,


01:16:11.390 --> 01:16:13.182
he will lose his power.


01:16:13.351 --> 01:16:14.726
Then I'll get rid of it.


01:16:15.269 --> 01:16:16.269
Hamsters…


01:16:16.687 --> 01:16:18.145
Run, Chickenhare!


01:16:18.314 --> 01:16:19.522
Attack!


01:16:34.705 --> 01:16:35.830
Now what?


01:16:36.415 --> 01:16:39.124
What are you waiting for?
Break that wall!


01:17:05.778 --> 01:17:08.528
Get the scepter, now,
before he throws it in the pit!


01:17:21.710 --> 01:17:23.377
Hamsters, the wheel!


01:17:32.513 --> 01:17:35.388
Okay, Chickenhare,
that's how you want to play it,


01:17:35.558 --> 01:17:38.349
then let's do it my way.


01:17:54.159 --> 01:17:55.201
How does it look?


01:17:59.331 --> 01:18:00.456
That wasn't there before.


01:18:15.347 --> 01:18:18.305
Hey rodents,
come and get us if you dare!


01:18:24.272 --> 01:18:25.481
Hi there.


01:19:00.558 --> 01:19:01.558
Look at him!


01:19:01.726 --> 01:19:05.143
Get me the scepter
if you want to fly another day.


01:19:17.867 --> 01:19:18.950
Come on!


01:19:33.883 --> 01:19:35.550
Game over, Lapin.


01:19:35.718 --> 01:19:38.968
No it's not,
we're just about to get started.


01:20:15.632 --> 01:20:17.466
Catch me if you can!


01:20:18.177 --> 01:20:20.969
- Let's finish this, Brother.
- Not so fast.


01:20:24.308 --> 01:20:25.600
Hamsters, charge!


01:20:31.983 --> 01:20:34.691
Finish him, Chickenhare's mine.


01:21:12.856 --> 01:21:14.356
Give me that!


01:21:31.124 --> 01:21:32.124
Good riddance.


01:21:54.314 --> 01:21:55.439
Uncle!


01:22:12.708 --> 01:22:14.749
I got you, come on.


01:22:21.591 --> 01:22:23.382
Chickenhare, no!


01:22:23.844 --> 01:22:26.760
Fly chicken, fly.


01:22:45.198 --> 01:22:49.365
If I'm going down,
at least I'm taking you with me.


01:22:54.499 --> 01:22:55.540
What?


01:22:55.708 --> 01:22:57.416
Impossible!


01:23:26.572 --> 01:23:28.364
Hey, guys, I'm back!


01:23:28.533 --> 01:23:30.199
Alright, you did it!


01:23:30.451 --> 01:23:32.910
Did you see that? I can fly!


01:23:33.579 --> 01:23:36.371
I wouldn't call that flying,
more like gliding.


01:23:36.832 --> 01:23:38.624
Abe, cork it, will you?


01:23:38.793 --> 01:23:40.001
Chickenhare,


01:23:40.169 --> 01:23:41.419
you found it.


01:23:42.171 --> 01:23:43.712
Yeah, but Lapin took it and…


01:23:43.881 --> 01:23:46.381
Not the Hamster of Darkness,
Chickenhare.


01:23:46.551 --> 01:23:47.759
You.


01:23:48.093 --> 01:23:49.343
You found you.


01:23:51.722 --> 01:23:53.097
I'm glad.


01:23:54.349 --> 01:23:55.933
Me too, Dad.


01:23:57.937 --> 01:24:00.187
A hare who can fly.


01:24:00.355 --> 01:24:01.897
How cool is this?


01:24:02.066 --> 01:24:05.482
What are you talking about?
He can fly because he's a chicken.


01:24:05.653 --> 01:24:07.236
What? He's a hare.


01:24:07.404 --> 01:24:08.404
- Chicken.
- Hare.


01:24:08.573 --> 01:24:09.698
- Chicken.
- Hare.


01:24:11.951 --> 01:24:13.451
So what'd I miss?


01:24:14.912 --> 01:24:16.204
Hey!


01:24:16.455 --> 01:24:18.330
What do you want from me?
I just…


01:24:25.380 --> 01:24:26.380
Chickenhare?


01:24:31.762 --> 01:24:32.762
Chickenhare.


01:24:33.680 --> 01:24:35.097
I knew it.


01:24:39.686 --> 01:24:42.228
Chickenhare, what are you doing?


01:24:42.689 --> 01:24:46.064
Guys, I just discovered the location
of the holy spork!


01:24:46.568 --> 01:24:48.360
We leave in 5 minutes.


01:24:48.528 --> 01:24:52.028
But they're just about to start
bringing out the hors d'oeuvres.


01:24:52.449 --> 01:24:53.991
But what about your induction?


01:24:54.159 --> 01:24:55.993
This is what you've wanted
your whole life.


01:24:56.161 --> 01:24:57.620
Sorry, Dad, don't have time.


01:24:57.787 --> 01:25:01.329
Hold on, Chickenhare.
You can't leave…


01:25:01.833 --> 01:25:02.958
without this.


01:25:08.798 --> 01:25:10.590
Your golden machete.


01:25:11.009 --> 01:25:12.967
You really mean this?


01:25:13.512 --> 01:25:15.345
I love you, Dad.


01:25:17.516 --> 01:25:20.391
Now, go get that holy spork.


01:25:36.326 --> 01:25:39.785
What are the odds
both of my best friends are masochists?


01:25:43.792 --> 01:25:44.792
Hey!

